{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119858","id":3766200018,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7ge6bS","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119858","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119858.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119858.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119858","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119858/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/119858/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119858/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/a148bbc35cc1ed25ff0092319f1d51e1656fbbbe","number":119858,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Replace `zlib` with `zlib-ng`","user":{"login":"DeeJayLSP","id":60024671,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMDI0Njcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60024671?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP","html_url":"https://github.com/DeeJayLSP","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DeeJayLSP/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"[zlib-ng](https://github.com/zlib-ng/zlib-ng) is a replacement for zlib that adds things for \"next generation\" systems like CPU intrinsics and other optimizations.\r\n\r\nI recently ran into it, found out some Linux distros like Fedora and Arch have been replacing zlib with it (as a package named `zlib-ng-compat`), and decided to try replacing Godot's built-in zlib with it.\r\n\r\nIt is compiled in compatibility mode (`ZLIB_COMPAT`), which effectively acts as a drop-in replacement for the standard zlib instead of a different library that coexists with it (of course, build system needs adjustments) and allows `builtin_zlib` to work as usual.\r\n\r\n- x86 in general implements **SSE2** instructions.\r\n- x86_64 adds **SSSE3**, **SSE4.1** and **SSE4.2** on top of that. **AVX2**, **AVX-512** and **(V)PCLMUL** are ignored.\r\n- ARM, both v7 and v8, only adds **NEON**, ignoring **ARMv6** (the only function already has a NEON version) and **CRC32** (too new) instructions.\r\n\r\n## Benchmarks\r\n\r\nI'm aware DEFLATE and gzip compression algorithms in Godot use zlib, so I experimented with both in a x86_64 machine.\r\n\r\nTest project: [compression_test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28374046/compression_test.zip)\r\n\r\nBuild command: `scons -j8 target=editor production=yes`\r\n\r\n### Results\r\n\r\nUsing default compression level in Project Settings. Iterations are in miliseconds. Lower is better.\r\n\r\n#### Compress DEFLATE\r\n|Build|1|2|3|4|\r\n|-|-|-|-|-|\r\n|master|1035.08|998.73|991.98|1003.36|\r\n|PR|1029.49|1027.55|1025.84|1031.75|\r\n\r\n#### Decompress DEFLATE\r\n|Build|1|2|3|4|\r\n|-|-|-|-|-|\r\n|master|19.06|18.24|18.03|17.97|\r\n|PR|7.42|7.83|7.55|7.5|\r\n\r\n#### Compress gzip\r\n|Build|1|2|3|4|\r\n|-|-|-|-|-|\r\n|master|999.07|1003.53|999.20|999.36|\r\n|PR|1033.61|1026.50|1029.05|1035.75|\r\n\r\n#### Decompress gzip\r\n|Build|1|2|3|4|\r\n|-|-|-|-|-|\r\n|master|24.24|24.01|24.20|23.55|\r\n|PR|10.39|10.13|10.27|10.10|\r\n\r\nOn a quick look, we can notice a tiny performance loss during compression (around 1.021-1.03x slower), but a **massive** gain during decompression (around 2.35-2.42x faster). I do believe this is a sacrifice worth making.\r\n\r\n## AI disclosure\r\n\r\nDuring some situations where compilation failed, I resorted to AI to find out what defines were correct. Some decisions I took actually go against what it told me to do.\r\n\r\nI also asked which ARM optimizations were valid to apply in the `arm` variants, as I'm only familiar that NEON should be applied for both (it suggested to add CRC32 for `arm64`, but I left it out for reasons already mentioned).\r\n\r\nApart from that, no lines have been written by AI.\r\n\r\nThe script in the test project, however, is mostly AI-generated, with some changes to make it more convenient for usage in a bash script.\r\n\r\nSince I had no way to test, I left optimizations for `ppc64` and `loongarch64` out.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471795,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE3OTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:thirdparty","name":"topic:thirdparty","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","description":"","color":"447777","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"ak